  "narrative": "Due validation: H89 asks whether feature_063=1 versus feature_063=0 is associated with a more negative outcome_001 value, i.e. stronger composite dependency, within the extreme low feature_040 band feature_040 <= -9. Returned values are already signed to the negative-direction hypothesis, so positive estimates indicate stronger dependency in the feature_063=1 group. Discovery R91 gave +0.161 [-0.024, 0.347], which is directionally meaningful at the point estimate but not conclusive because the interval includes zero and values below the 0.15-unit threshold. The newly released independent validation R140 gave +0.315 [0.072, 0.558] under the stringent independent alpha, with cell sizes 91 and 491. This strengthens the directional association: the validation interval excludes zero and the point estimate is well above the threshold. However, the validation lower bound remains below 0.15, so the isolated H89 context does not establish threshold exceeding with high precision. I therefore keep H89 accepted as a supported dataset-specific association in the low feature_040 band, especially because H115 (the broader feature_040 <= -7 band) was independently validated with lower bound above threshold, while flagging that the exact effect size in the <= -9 subset remains uncertain. No new validation can be requested; this is observational and label-opaque, not causal or mechanistic. I also closed H148 because its accepted feature_063-by-feature_038>=0 interaction (R153 +0.559 [0.387, 0.731]) is sufficiently supported for the current observational synthesis and validation budget is exhausted. I closed low-priority unresolved no-evidence items H114 and H122 to prioritize the remaining pending feature_063 context-localization analyses. Current supported dataset-specific findings remain: feature_037=1 is associated with markedly stronger dependency (validated positive signed estimate approximately +0.831); feature_027=1 is associated with markedly stronger dependency (validated approximately +0.768); feature_002=1 is associated with weaker dependency (validated approximately +0.781); feature_010=1 is associated with weaker dependency (validated approximately +0.378); and feature_063=1 is associated with stronger dependency overall and in several contexts, including validated low feature_040 bands and a formally accepted interaction showing concentration in the feature_038 >= 0 context. Important negative findings include null or rejected main effects and interactions for the constructed markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015; rejected feature_046 contrasts tested so far; rejected interactions among core binary predictors apart from feature_063-by-feature_038>=0; and rejected or unsupported feature_063 effects in some contexts such as feature_038 <= 0, feature_018 >= 0, and the middle feature_040 band. Unresolved items include the weak feature_063 signal in feature_036 >= 0 (H154), pending decomposition of the positive feature_038 context by feature_037, feature_018, and feature_036, and whether the feature_063-feature_038 interaction persists or disappears inside the low feature_040 band. The most informative next analyses are the registered feature_063 context tests H160-H167, plus the two new proposals here: a direct feature_063 mean difference within feature_038 >= 0 and feature_040 <= -7, and an interaction of feature_063 by feature_038 >= 0 restricted to the low feature_040 band. These will help determine whether the accepted feature_038 interaction is robust, confounded or confounded-with feature_040, or context-specific. All conclusions remain observational dataset-specific associations with opaque predictor labels; they do not establish causality, independence from unmeasured factors, biological mechanism, or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after H89 validation. H89 accepted but threshold-uncertain: feature_063=1 vs 0 in feature_040 <= -9, signed discovery +0.161 [-0.024,0.347], validation +0.315 [0.072,0.558]; validation excludes zero and strengthens direction, but lower bound is below 0.15, so exact threshold exceedance in the extreme band is not definitive. The broader validated H115 low feature_040 <= -7 estimate (+0.375 [0.198,0.552]) supports the general low-band context. Closed H148 (accepted feature_063-by-feature_038>=0 interaction, R153 +0.559 [0.387,0.731]) because validation budget exhausted. Closed H114 and H122 as low-priority unresolved/no-evidence to prioritize active feature_063 context tests. Supported core observational associations: feature_037=1 stronger dependency (validated ~+0.831); feature_027=1 stronger dependency (validated ~+0.768); feature_002=1 weaker dependency (validated ~+0.781); feature_010=1 weaker dependency (validated ~+0.378); feature_063=1 stronger dependency overall and in validated low feature_040 contexts, with accepted interaction concentrating in feature_038>=0. Negative/unsupported: feature_007, feature_058, feature_015 main effects and their tested interactions; feature_031/feature_006 after validation; feature_046 tested contrasts; feature_063 in feature_038<=0, feature_018>=0, and middle feature_040 band; interactions among feature_037/027/002/010 and assay halves. Unresolved: H154 weak feature_063 in feature_036>=0; pending H160-H167 context decomposition; new proposals test combined positive feature_038 plus low feature_040 and whether the feature_038 interaction persists within low feature_040. Next analysis priority: these feature_063-feature_038-feature_040 interactions/combined-context means, followed by decomposition of positive feature_038 by feature_037/018/036. No causality, biology, independence, or generalizability claims."
